openfasttrace (4.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * This release includes several usability improvements to the
    requirement ID and other syntax used in OpenFastTrace. For example,
    the hash mark (#) can now be used in addition to the tilde (~) as a
    revision separator. This prevents situations where the name part of
    the ID is displayed as cross-out text in Markdown. Of course, the
    previous double-tilde syntax remains valid.
  * The source tag importer now supports JSX (.jsx) and TSX (.tsx)
    source files, the file types of React components written in
    JavaScript and TypeScript.
  * #638: Allow hash mark in addition to tilde as revision separator
  * #647: Add support for JSX and TSX in the source tag importer
  * #561: Build and publish native binaries for Linux (x64 and arm64),
    Windows (x64) and macOS (arm64)

 -- itsallcode.org <maintainers@itsallcode.org>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:20:06 +0100

openfasttrace (4.11.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * OFT now allows embedders to pass plugin JARs to OFT at runtime
    through the Java API, so plugins
  * resolved through an external dependency mechanism no longer need to
    be installed in the
  * predefined plugin directory.
  * The source tag importer now supports Visual Basic (.vb) source
    files.
  * The user guide documentation now has automatic lateral navigation.
  * #610: Allow adding plugins via configuration using
    `Oft.builder().addPlugin(name, jars...)`
  * #612: Add support for Visual Basic in the source tag importer
  * #401: Added regression test for RST parser corner case (issue was
    fixed already)
  * #423: Fixed tag parsing inconsistency in Markdown and
    reStructuredText importers
  * #574: Fixed invalid HTML when inline code contains underscores
  * #604: Fixed link to Product Lifecycle in SECURITY.md
  * #605: Added automatic lateral navigation to the user guide
    documentation
  * #606: Fixed typo in AGENTS.md for "functions"
  * #608: Fixed formatting and updated links in README.md
  * #614: Fixed markdown syntax in the AI agent skill

 -- itsallcode.org <maintainers@itsallcode.org>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:55:04 +0200

openfasttrace (4.9.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Importers for long coverage tags, Markdown and reStructuredText now
    collect the location of coverage IDs in documents and source code.
  * The exact location of an item ID is required for IDE plugins in
    order to support features like syntax highlighting, find
    occurrences, jump to definition and auto-complete. Adding this
    feature to OFT helps avoid code duplications and improves
    reliability.
  * Deprecated ImportEventListener methods: setId,
    addCoveredId, and addDependsOnId.
  * #570: Collect source code location of specification item IDs

 -- itsallcode.org <maintainers@itsallcode.org>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 17:34:13 +0200

